{#
_avatar_picker.html.twig — the profile picture: the one in use, and choosing a
new one from a connected service.

Shared by the setup wizard and Settings → Profile, because they are two views of
the same thing. Only the URLs differ, so the caller passes them:

  sources    list<Integration>   connections that can supply a picture
  picking    Integration|null    the one whose pictures are on screen
  entries    list<Entry>         images from it
  pickUrls   map id => url       where "browse this one" goes
  closeUrl   string              where "stop browsing" goes
  fileField  string              full_name of the form field the choice binds to
  current    string|null         URL of the picture in use, if there is one
  modalPicker bool               open the file picker in a dialog (see below)

Two ways to choose, because the two callers differ in where they live.

Settings passes `modalPicker`: each connection opens the same dialog the compose
window attaches files with, in its avatar mode, and the choice comes back through
settings/avatar_from_service_controller.js on the form. `picking`, `entries`,
`pickUrls`, `closeUrl` and `fileField` are not used.

The setup wizard does not, and still gets the grid below. Its profile step is
itself rendered in the modal frame, which the file picker would replace — the
wizard would vanish behind it. A thumbnail *is* the submit there: choosing and
saving are one action, and the button carries the field name the form binds it
to. Browsing is a navigation rather than a client-side toggle because these
fields belong to the surrounding form, and HTML has no nested forms.
#}
{% if current is defined and current is not null %}
    {# Shown wherever the profile is edited. A file input reports a filename at
       best, so without this there is no way to tell what the picture currently
       is — only that there is one. #}
    <div class="mt-5 flex items-center gap-3">
        <img src="{{ current }}"
             alt=""
             class="size-12 rounded-full object-cover border border-line">
        <span class="text-xs text-ink-faint">{{ 'profile.avatar_current'|trans }}</span>
    </div>
{% endif %}

{% if sources|length %}
    <div class="mt-5 pt-5 border-t border-line">
        <p class="text-[13px] font-medium text-ink-soft">{{ 'profile.avatar_from.heading'|trans }}</p>

        <div class="mt-2 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2">
            {% for source in sources %}
                {% if modalPicker|default(false) %}
                    {# type=button: this sits inside the profile form, where the
                       default would submit it. #}
                    <button type="button"
                            id="avatar-source-{{ source.id }}"
                            data-controller="ui--modal"
                            data-ui--modal-title-value="{{ source.name }}"
                            data-ui--modal-size-value="{{ source.provider.isMediaLibrary ? 'full' : 'wide' }}"
                            data-ui--modal-src-value="{{ path('app_integration_browse', { id: source.id, mode: 'avatar' }) }}"
                            data-action="click->ui--modal#open"
                            class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 h-8 px-3 rounded-lg text-sm font-medium border transition-colors cursor-pointer
                                   border-field bg-field text-ink-soft hover:bg-hover">
                        <i class="{{ source.provider.icon }} text-xs" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                        {{ source.name }}
                    </button>
                {% else %}
                    {% set isOpen = picking is not null and picking.id == source.id %}
                    <a href="{{ isOpen ? closeUrl : pickUrls[source.id] }}"
                       data-turbo-frame="{{ frame|default('_self') }}"
                       id="avatar-source-{{ source.id }}"
                       class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 h-8 px-3 rounded-lg text-sm font-medium border transition-colors
                              {% if isOpen %}
                                border-accent bg-accent/10 text-accent
                              {% else %}
                                border-field bg-field text-ink-soft hover:bg-hover
                              {% endif %}">
                        <i class="{{ source.provider.icon }} text-xs" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                        {{ source.name }}
                    </a>
                {% endif %}
            {% endfor %}
        </div>

        {% if not modalPicker|default(false) and picking is not null %}
            {% if entries|length %}
                <ul class="mt-4 grid grid-cols-4 sm:grid-cols-6 gap-2">
                    {% for entry in entries %}
                        <li>
                            <button type="submit"
                                    name="{{ fileField }}"
                                    value="{{ entry.id }}"
                                    title="{{ entry.name }}"
                                    class="block w-full aspect-square overflow-hidden rounded-lg border border-line
                                           hover:border-accent focus:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-accent
                                           transition-colors cursor-pointer">
                                <img src="{{ path('app_integration_thumbnail', { id: picking.id, file: entry.id }) }}"
                                     alt="{{ entry.name }}"
                                     loading="lazy"
                                     class="w-full h-full object-cover">
                            </button>
                        </li>
                    {% endfor %}
                </ul>
            {% else %}
                <p class="mt-4 text-xs text-ink-faint">{{ 'profile.avatar_from.empty'|trans }}</p>
            {% endif %}
        {% endif %}
    </div>
{% endif %}
